BUAT RINGKASAN

Market Stage: Growth (Pre-TGE / Post-Launch Scaling)
Primary Category: Memecoin Launchpad / Fair Launch Platform
Competitor Count: 8 major competitors identified (Meteora, Raydium, SunPump, PinkSale, Moonshot, Bonk.fun, Clanker, Four.meme)
Major Narrative: Memecoin Supercycle / Fair Launch Platform (Main); App-Specific AMM Vertical Integration (Secondary)
Trading Availability: Native on PumpSwap (Solana, Base, Blast); Aggregated via Jupiter (Solana); Legacy on Raydium (Solana); Individual tokens on various CEXs
Adoption Metrics Available: TVL, Daily Active Users, Transactions, Volume, Revenue, Tokens Created, Graduate Rate — all via DefiLlama, Token Terminal, Dune Analytics

---

Open Threads

- Verified contract addresses for Pump.fun bonding curve and PumpSwap on Base and Blast — Phase 3 and Phase 4 used placeholder URLs `https://basescan.org/address/0x...` and `https://blastscan.io/address/0x...`; need actual verified addresses
- Exact TVL/volume/revenue split by chain (Solana vs Base vs Blast) — DefiLlama shows aggregate; chain-level breakdown needed for precise market share
- Mobile app download/active user numbers — Apple/Google Play Store don't publish exact install counts; SensorTower/Data.ai estimates not verified
- Graduate rate methodology — "1-2%" cited from community Dune dashboards; need official or cross-verified methodology
- PumpSwap fee split detail — 1% trading fee: how much to protocol vs LP vs other; not documented publicly
- Raydium legacy pool volume vs PumpSwap volume post-migration — Dune dashboards exist but need cross-verification
- Base/Blast adoption metrics vs Solana — Base growing fast post-Mar 2025; Blast lower; need time-series comparison
- Competitor volume market share on Base (Clanker, Four.meme vs Pump.fun Base) — multi-chain launchpad comparison needed
- Regulatory status impact on market access — no legal entity disclosed; potential geographic restrictions not mapped
- Fee collector treasury size and composition — Phase 5 used placeholder; need verified on-chain balances across 3 chains
- Token TGE probability and timeline — purely speculative; no official signal; market prices in expectation but unconfirmed
- PumpSwap AMM type confirmation — CPMM vs CLMM; Phase 4 says constant product but not explicitly verified on-chain
- Historical revenue data granularity — Token Terminal/DefiLlama show charts but raw data export access unclear
- Cross-chain user overlap — how many wallets use Pump.fun on multiple chains; not tracked publicly
- Institutional/whale usage vs retail — wallet size distribution of traders; not published